<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">When Johnny Comes Marching Home</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1863">1863</a> (deposited in the Library of Congress on 26 September <a href="/years/1863">1863</a>)</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;When Johnny Comes Marching Home&quot; was written during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a> by the Irish-American bandleader Patrick Gilmore. Its first edition was deposited in the Library of Congress on 26 September 1863, with words and music credited to &quot;Louis Lambert&quot;; the publisher, Henry Tolman &amp; Co. of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a>, kept the copyright.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>&quot;<b>When Johnny Comes Marching Home</b>&quot; was written during the American Civil War by the Irish-American bandleader Patrick Gilmore.</blockquote><a href="/songs/when-johnny-comes-marching-home">When Johnny Comes Marching Home</a></li></ul></section>
